     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On Fri, May 15, 2015 at 5:23 PM, Mark Miller &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mamil...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; disclaimer:  crossposted from stackoverflow.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I have made some (functional) shiny interfaces in which a reactive data\r<br>&gt; object was used as the data argument inside of renderDataTable.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; dataSel4counts &lt;- reactive({\r<br>&gt;   if(input$targspec != &#39;&lt;ALL&gt;&#39;) {\r<br>&gt;     tsFilter &lt;- lendata$targ.spec == input$targspec\r<br>&gt;   } else {\r<br>&gt;     tsFilter &lt;- rep(TRUE, length(lendata$targ.spec))\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt;   lendata[ lendata$adjp &lt;= input$maxp &amp; tsFilter ,  ]\r<br>&gt; })\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; output$countTable = renderDataTable({\r<br>&gt;   data &lt;- dataSel4counts()\r<br>&gt;   datatable(\r<br>&gt;     data\r<br>&gt;   )\r<br>&gt; })\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Recently I added several of the extensions documented\r<br>&gt; onhttps://<a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/DT/extensions.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/DT/extensions.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398760952000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2TJoFYREGe1FLpeaprT6HY\">rstudio.github.io/DT/extensions.html</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I get the sense that (by default) client-side processing is a consequence of\r<br>&gt; adding DT extensions.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I would like to switch back to server side processing, following\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/DT/server.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/DT/server.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398760952000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1of95iIgjn9Ny6LM836Bxv\">http://rstudio.github.io/DT/server.html</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; But it seems like the data arguments (iris in the example) can&#39;t be\r<br>&gt; reactive. When I try to do something like\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; action = dataTableAjax(session, dataSel4counts())\r<br>&gt; widget = datatable(dataSel4counts(), server = TRUE, options = list(\r<br>&gt;   ajax = list(url = action)\r<br>&gt; ))\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I get a variety of errors, including\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Warning in run(timeoutMs) : You are using the server-side processing mode,\r<br>&gt; but did not specify the &#39;ajax&#39; option. See\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/DT/server.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/DT/server.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398760952000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1of95iIgjn9Ny6LM836Bxv\">http://rstudio.github.io/DT/server.html</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Error in .getReactiveEnvironment()$currentContext() : Operation not allowed\r<br>&gt; without an active reactive context. (You tried to do something that can only\r<br>&gt; be done from inside a reactive expression or observer.)\r<br>"
    ]
